      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "RFC: add local adaptive-refresh replay tooling",
        "body": "## Decision requested\n\nShould CodexBar upstream own an offline CLI for comparing refresh policies against a caller-supplied JSONL trace?\n\nThe supporting `AdaptiveReplayKit` target is package-internal. This PR adds one executable product, `AdaptiveReplayCLI`. It does not change Adaptive, make it the default, or add a production signal.\n\nRefs #1739 and #1861.\n\n## Scope after review\n\nCopilot and ClawSweeper identified two concrete problems in the previous revision: CRLF records were not parsed correctly, and the branch mixed offline analysis with runtime collection and transcript metadata access.\n\nThis revision is rebased onto current `main` and narrows the diff from 32 files and +4,147/-55 to 21 files and +2,840/-7. It removes:\n\n- app-side trace recording and every `Sources/CodexBar` hook;\n- transcript-directory scanning and activity collection;\n- the persistent trace writer and storage contract;\n- recorder, writer, and activity-probe tests;\n- the unrelated Keychain test adjustment.\n\nThere are no changes under `Sources/CodexBar`, and the app target's dependencies are unchanged. Of the 2,840 additions, 1,516 are the offline implementation, 1,224 are tests, and 100 are package or documentation changes.\n\nThe remaining code is:\n\n- a Foundation-only schema, strict and tolerant JSONL parsers, replay engine, policy models, segmentation, metrics, and schedule audit;\n- a package-internal library target and one CLI product;\n- six platform-independent test files plus a macOS-only parity test against the production Adaptive policy;\n- an evidence-only update to the existing decision record.\n\nThe parser now splits records with `Character.isNewline`, which handles Swift's CRLF grapheme correctly. Strict and tolerant multi-record CRLF regression tests cover the two Copilot findings.\n\n## Data boundary\n\nThe CLI reads an explicit trace path and writes a report to stdout. This PR has no app-side recorder, trace writer, storage lifecycle, transcript scanning or collection, provider calls, network path, or production-policy change. Optional activity fields are input-only. No trace or fixture is committed.\n\nRuntime capture and its privacy/lifecycle contract are deliberately out of scope and can be proposed separately if the offline tool is accepted.\n\n## Author-run replay evidence\n\nExact head: `cd96204ac197ec0c7ce48e615a608358c01ba3fb`\n\nThe local input has 1,780 records and SHA-256 `b1e4aa33180b7c177293eb9ed16b45e24e026d259600fba2b1b67b931b904f0b`. The raw trace remains local.\n\n| Policy | Simulated refreshes | Per observed 24h | Simulated advances | Unconstrained active over 5m | Menu staleness p50 / p95 |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Current Adaptive | 694 | 143.47 | 53 | 4 / 145 | 142s / 1093s |\n| Activity-cap candidate | 696 | 143.88 | 53 | 0 / 145 | 139s / 1093s |\n| Fixed 5m | 1,383 | 285.90 | 0 | 0 / 99 | 150s / 281s |\n\nThe run found 28 observed segments and excluded 26.10 hours with a five-minute legacy-gap heuristic. Activity fields were present for 462 of 733 decisions; 185 of those 462 samples were inside the five-minute active window. The trace contains 46 recorded advances and zero timer-advance evaluations.\n\nOn this input, current Adaptive schedules 49.8% fewer simulated refreshes than fixed five minutes. The candidate adds two refreshes and removes four active-delay violations, but neither Adaptive variant improves p95 staleness. This supports evaluating the tooling; it does not support a default or production-policy change.\n\n## Validation\n\nFor exact head `cd96204a`:\n\n- `make check` passed: SwiftFormat 0/1,372 and SwiftLint 0 violations in 1,371 files.\n- `swift package describe` exposes `AdaptiveReplayCLI` but not `AdaptiveReplayKit` as a product.\n- `swift build --product AdaptiveReplayCLI` passed.\n- `swift run AdaptiveReplayCLI <hash-pinned-trace>` produced the table above and the segmentation/audit totals.\n\nThe previous pushed revision, `d394420d`, has identical source and test code and passed the full 610 selections in 51/51 groups, 54 offline replay tests, 16 parser tests, and 3 production-policy parity tests. The only tree change in `cd96204a` is removing the public `AdaptiveReplayKit` product declaration. Upstream CI is running the exact head.\n\n## Limitations\n\n- This is author-run evidence from one machine, not an independently reproducible dataset.\n- Gap segmentation is heuristic and cannot identify sleep, reboot, a long refresh, or an event-loop stall.\n- The trace predates evaluation records, so accepted versus rejected live evaluations cannot be audited.\n- The result does not measure battery use, elapsed user time, provider requests, or cost.\n- Both Adaptive variants have worse p95 menu staleness than fixed five minutes on this trace.\n\nThe review question is intentionally narrow: should this repository own the offline CLI and its package-internal replay target?\n",
